WEBVTT

00:07:58.657 --> 00:08:00.815
(Laughter)

00:08:00.839 --> 00:08:02.003
Why?

00:08:02.027 --> 00:08:03.901
"Because of this person in front of me.

00:08:03.925 --> 00:08:05.918
This is not a person, this is a monster."

00:08:05.942 --> 00:08:06.942
(Laughter)

00:08:06.966 --> 00:08:10.480
And this monster is here
just to ruin your life.

00:08:10.504 --> 00:08:11.894
(Laughter)

00:08:11.918 --> 00:08:13.767
Now that thought process,

00:08:13.791 --> 00:08:18.497
it's called catastrophizing,
the one where we make the worst of things.

00:08:18.521 --> 00:08:21.252
And it's one of the primary
types of thoughts that we know

00:08:21.276 --> 00:08:22.941
is associated with chronic anger.

00:08:22.965 --> 00:08:25.037
But there's a couple of others.

00:08:25.061 --> 00:08:26.625
Misattributing causation.

00:08:26.649 --> 00:08:29.426
Angry people tend to put blame
where it doesn't belong.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.332
Not just on people,